+# Source-only apply / rollback package
+Base exact production image downloads-56fc79f / local commit56fc79fb554e97dc89ae88688a1ca79369136d7a. Each changed file preimage is in manifest. No deploy performed.
+Before future apply, verify exact preimage hashes, protect old image/env backup and current order aggregate. Apply only reviewed 5-file source patch in a build checkout; no migrations, Caddy, dispatcher, WDTT or adapter changes. Build/release remains root responsibility.
+PLATEGA_CREATE_ENABLED defaults true; set false in actual backend environment for cutover, preserve PLATEGA_ENABLED=true and merchant/auth config. Existing process config needs controlled backend rollout; no production action authorized by this package. Hide-only per-button flags are optional separate UI delta; turning them off also makes cached handler reuse inaccessible, so they are deliberately NOT part of required env delta. Gate false already prevents new records/POST on cached Telegram/WebApp requests.
+After runtime acceptance, creation is closed while existing status/callback/reconciliation/reuse continue. No old payment row deletion or status rewrite.
+Rollback of the feature: restore PLATEGA_CREATE_ENABLED=true/default and reviewed old image/source/env only when root explicitly chooses to reopen old purchases; preserve all existing/new owner order routing and transaction IDs. Do not restore callback topology blindly. A broken creation release can stay false while source is corrected; callback/VPN must stay operational. Unknown expired-trial→paid defect in old wdtt_direct.py remains unchanged, not transplanted into new TEST.
+Checks: python3 review/test_create_gate_offline.py executes real AST-extracted source functions, fake DB/provider IO. 12 unittest cases + 5 outer WebApp subcases; no sockets. Syntax/diff and unchanged AST proof. Full dependency-import pytest/mypy/frontend gates not run: local aiogram/sqlalchemy dependency environment missing; offline uv cache insufficient. No package downloads/provider/network calls made. The scoped test is not a full production/framework integration claim.
